Architecture plan for mike-t-302f-test-website-004

Issues in scope:
- #1 Initialize Next.js project (App Router + TypeScript)

Module structure and file organization:
- Use a Next.js App Router application at the repository root.
- Place route files under `app/`, starting with `app/layout.tsx`, `app/page.tsx`, and `app/globals.css`.
- Keep static assets in `public/`.
- Add project configuration at the root: `package.json`, `next.config.*`, `tsconfig.json`, and lint/config files as needed by the selected Next.js scaffold.
- If shared code becomes necessary in later issues, prefer `src/components/`, `src/lib/`, and `src/types/` for reusable UI, utilities, and shared TypeScript types. For issue #1, avoid premature abstractions unless generated by the scaffold.

Dependencies between issues:
- Issue #1 is foundational and has no implementation dependency on other issues.
- Later issues should build on the App Router structure and root layout created in issue #1.

Key design decisions:
- Use TypeScript from the start for typed React components and configuration.
- Use the App Router rather than the legacy Pages Router.
- Keep the initial application minimal: root layout, homepage route, global stylesheet, and standard Next.js build scripts.
- Commit only repository setup artifacts in this setup session; implement the actual Next.js scaffold during the issue-specific session.
